From: Ferrite overlay
Subject: [PATCH] std/start.zig: export Ferrite's _start when std.os.ferrite present

When our overlay layers `std.os.ferrite` into the std tree, divert the
comptime entry-point dispatch to export Ferrite's `_start` (naked, per
arch) and `ferriteStartShim` (the trampoline that populates
`std.os.ferrite.argv` and calls `root.main`). Both live in our overlay
at `std/os/ferrite/start.zig`.

Gate is `@hasDecl(std.os, "ferrite")` rather than `native_os ==
.ferrite` because stock nix-released Zig 0.16.0's compiler doesn't
know about a `.ferrite` target string; today the compiler reports
`builtin.os.tag = .freestanding` for our builds. The hasDecl check
catches our overlay regardless of which tag the compiler picked.

--- a/std/start.zig
+++ b/std/start.zig
@@ -62,6 +62,12 @@
             // Only call main when defined. For WebAssembly it's allowed to pass `-fno-entry` in which
             // case it's not required to provide an entrypoint such as main.
             if (!@hasDecl(root, start_sym_name) and @hasDecl(root, "main")) @export(&wasm_freestanding_start, .{ .name = start_sym_name });
+        } else if (@hasDecl(std.os, "ferrite")) {
+            // Ferrite freestanding boot — overlay-provided naked _start
+            // parses argc/argv off the stack and calls ferriteStartShim.
+            if (!@hasDecl(root, start_sym_name) and @hasDecl(root, "main")) {
+                @export(&std.os.ferrite.start._start, .{ .name = start_sym_name, .linkage = .strong });
+            }
         } else switch (native_os) {
             .other, .freestanding, .@"3ds", .psp, .vita => {},
             else => if (!@hasDecl(root, start_sym_name)) @export(&_start, .{ .name = start_sym_name }),
